# Testing: Verify What, Not How

When writing or reviewing tests:

- **Verify What (results):** Assert on observable outcomes — return values, public state, UI output, API responses. Focus on behavior the caller sees.
- **Do not verify How (implementation):** Avoid asserting on internal variables, private methods, implementation-specific call order, or module internals. Refactoring implementation should not break tests.

## Examples

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD — verifies outcome
expect(component.getByRole('button', { name: /save/i })).toBeInTheDocument();
expect(validateFileName('valid.txt')).toBeNull();

// ❌ BAD — verifies implementation
expect(component.state.count).toBe(1);
expect(mockFn.mock.calls[0][1]).toEqual({ x: 1 });
```

See [docs/TESTING_STRATEGY.md](docs/TESTING_STRATEGY.md) for full black-box testing guidance.
